IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 2, ss 8E to 8H -- the savings for advocates and solicitors and for banks, insurers and
-- financial institutions, the Minister's power to investigate, and the secrecy of what s 8A and s 8B obtain. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- s 9 is the keel's and is shown repealed.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".

§ `Section 8E: advocates and solicitors`

-- src:2664 | 8E. Nothing in sections 8A and 8B compels the production by an
-- src:2665 | advocate and solicitor of a document containing a privileged
-- src:2666 | communication made by or to him or her in that capacity or
-- src:2667 | authorises the taking of possession of any such document which is in
-- src:2668 | his or her possession but if the advocate and solicitor refuses to
-- src:2669 | produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the
@ref s 8E (src:2664-2669)
GIVEN `the person is an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8E section 8A compels the advocate and solicitor to produce the document` MEANS
    IF `the person is an advocate and solicitor` AND `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 8A and 8B compels the production by an advocate and solicitor of a document containing a privileged communication made by or to him or her in that capacity" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving speaks only of an advocate and solicitor and a document containing a privileged communication made by or to him or her in that capacity

-- src:2664 | 8E. Nothing in sections 8A and 8B compels the production by an
-- src:2665 | advocate and solicitor of a document containing a privileged
-- src:2666 | communication made by or to him or her in that capacity or
-- src:2667 | authorises the taking of possession of any such document which is in
-- src:2668 | his or her possession but if the advocate and solicitor refuses to
-- src:2669 | produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the
@ref s 8E (src:2664-2669)
GIVEN `the person is an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document containing a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity is in the possession of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8E section 8B authorises the taking of possession of the document` MEANS
    IF `the person is an advocate and solicitor` AND `the document containing a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity is in the possession of the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 8A and 8B ... authorises the taking of possession of any such document which is in his or her possession" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving speaks only of such a document in the possession of the advocate and solicitor

-- "if the advocate and solicitor refuses to produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the name and address (if he or she knows them)":
-- a duty gated by "if" and qualified by "(if he or she knows them)"; a failed gate answers JUST FALSE (a duty: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2664 | 8E. Nothing in sections 8A and 8B compels the production by an
-- src:2665 | advocate and solicitor of a document containing a privileged
-- src:2666 | communication made by or to him or her in that capacity or
-- src:2667 | authorises the taking of possession of any such document which is in
-- src:2668 | his or her possession but if the advocate and solicitor refuses to
-- src:2669 | produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the
-- src:2674 | name and address (if he or she knows them) of the person to whom or
-- src:2675 | by or on behalf of whom the communication was made.
@ref s 8E (src:2664-2675)
GIVEN `the advocate and solicitor refuses to produce a document containing a privileged communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advocate and solicitor knows the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8E the advocate and solicitor is obliged to give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` MEANS
    IF `the advocate and solicitor refuses to produce a document containing a privileged communication` AND `the advocate and solicitor knows the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the advocate and solicitor refuses to produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the name and address (if he or she knows them)" -- the duty is gated by the refusal and by knowing the name and address (a duty whose "if" is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 8E act` IS ONE OF
    `s 8E give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`

-- A MUST with no time limit and no consequence the text states: no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:2664 | 8E. Nothing in sections 8A and 8B compels the production by an
-- src:2665 | advocate and solicitor of a document containing a privileged
-- src:2666 | communication made by or to him or her in that capacity or
-- src:2667 | authorises the taking of possession of any such document which is in
-- src:2668 | his or her possession but if the advocate and solicitor refuses to
-- src:2669 | produce the document he or she is nevertheless obliged to give the
-- src:2674 | name and address (if he or she knows them) of the person to whom or
-- src:2675 | by or on behalf of whom the communication was made.
@ref s 8E (src:2664-2675)
GIVEN `the name of the advocate and solicitor` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8E act`
`s 8E the advocate and solicitor who refuses to produce the document must give the name and address` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the advocate and solicitor`
    MUST `s 8E give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the advocate and solicitor` BECAUSE "the advocate and solicitor who refused to produce the document did not give the name and address"

§ `Section 8F: investigation of certain matters`

-- "Without limiting the powers conferred upon the Minister under section 8A, where the Minister has reason to suspect ... the Minister may make such investigation as he or she thinks expedient":
-- a grant gated by "where": the periods ruling (b) says JUST FALSE when the gate fails (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1).
-- src:2679 | 8F. Without limiting the powers conferred upon the Minister under
-- src:2680 | section 8A, where the Minister has reason to suspect that a person has
-- src:2681 | committed an offence under this Act, the Minister may make such
-- src:2682 | investigation as he or she thinks expedient for the due administration
-- src:2683 | of this Act.
@ref s 8F (src:2679-2683)
GIVEN `the Minister has reason to suspect that a person has committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8F the Minister has power under this section to investigate` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has reason to suspect that a person has committed an offence under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Minister has reason to suspect that a person has committed an offence under this Act, the Minister may make such investigation as he or she thinks expedient" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1; the section says "Without limiting the powers conferred upon the Minister under section 8A", so section 8A may still apply)

§ `Section 8G: banks, insurers and certain financial institutions`

-- The body is a "banking corporation" by the keel's definition (s 4(1)); the other two classes are facts the person states.
-- src:2688 | 8G. Nothing in section 8A authorises the Minister to call for the
-- src:2689 | production of books of a banking corporation or of any company
-- src:2690 | carrying on insurance business or of any financial institution that is
-- src:2691 | subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under
-- src:2692 | sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022 and
-- src:2693 | nothing in section 8F authorises the Minister to conduct an
-- src:2694 | investigation into any such corporation, company or financial
-- src:2695 | institution.
@ref s 8G (src:2688-2695)
GIVEN `the body is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company carries on insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a financial institution that is subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8G section 8A authorises the Minister to call for the production of the books` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "banking corporation" the body is a banking corporation` `the body is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the company carries on insurance business`
       OR `the institution is a financial institution that is subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 8A authorises the Minister to call for the production of books of a banking corporation or of any company carrying on insurance business or of any financial institution that is subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving speaks only of those three classes; section 8A is not limited for any other body by this section

-- src:2688 | 8G. Nothing in section 8A authorises the Minister to call for the
-- src:2689 | production of books of a banking corporation or of any company
-- src:2690 | carrying on insurance business or of any financial institution that is
-- src:2691 | subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under
-- src:2692 | sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022 and
-- src:2693 | nothing in section 8F authorises the Minister to conduct an
-- src:2694 | investigation into any such corporation, company or financial
-- src:2695 | institution.
@ref s 8G (src:2688-2695)
GIVEN `the body is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company carries on insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a financial institution that is subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8G section 8F authorises the Minister to conduct an investigation into the corporation, company or institution` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "banking corporation" the body is a banking corporation` `the body is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the company carries on insurance business`
       OR `the institution is a financial institution that is subject to control by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under sections 3 and 4 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in section 8F authorises the Minister to conduct an investigation into any such corporation, company or financial institution" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving speaks only of those three classes

§ `Section 8H: security of information`

-- (1) as a bar: "No information or document ... obtained under section 8A or 8B may, without the previous consent in writing of that corporation, be published or disclosed,
-- except to the Minister, the Registrar of Companies and their officers or to an inspector appointed under Part 9, unless the publication or disclosure is required --"
-- JUST TRUE means the bar applies; JUST FALSE is an exception the text states in its own words; NOTHING is information the bar does not speak of.
-- src:2701 | 8H.—(1) No information or document relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2702 | corporation which has been obtained under section 8A or 8B may,
-- src:2703 | without the previous consent in writing of that corporation, be
-- src:2704 | published or disclosed, except to the Minister, the Registrar of
-- src:2705 | Companies and their officers or to an inspector appointed under
-- src:2706 | Part 9, unless the publication or disclosure is required —
-- src:2708 | (a) with a view to the institution of or otherwise for the
-- src:2709 | purposes of, any criminal proceedings pursuant to, or
-- src:2710 | arising out of this Act or any criminal proceedings for an
-- src:2711 | offence entailing misconduct in connection with the
-- src:2712 | management of the corporation’s affairs or
-- src:2713 | misapplication or wrongful retention of its property;
-- src:2715 | (b) for the purpose of complying with any requirement or
-- src:2716 | exercising any power imposed or conferred by this Act in
-- src:2721 | connection with reports made by inspectors appointed
-- src:2722 | under Part 9;
-- src:2724 | (c) with a view to the institution by the Minister of
-- src:2725 | proceedings for the winding up of companies under this
-- src:2726 | Act of the corporation; or
-- src:2728 | (d) for the purpose of proceedings under section 8A or 8B.
@ref s 8H(1) (src:2701-2728)
GIVEN `the information or document relates to the affairs of a corporation and was obtained under section 8A or 8B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the previous consent in writing of the corporation has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication or disclosure is to the Minister, the Registrar of Companies, their officers or an inspector appointed under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication or disclosure is required with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, criminal proceedings pursuant to or arising out of this Act, or criminal proceedings for an offence entailing misconduct in connection with the management of the corporation's affairs or misapplication or wrongful retention of its property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication or disclosure is required for the purpose of complying with a requirement or exercising a power imposed or conferred by this Act in connection with reports made by inspectors appointed under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication or disclosure is required with a view to the institution by the Minister of proceedings for the winding up of the corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication or disclosure is required for the purpose of proceedings under section 8A or 8B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8H(1) the publication or disclosure is barred` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information or document relates to the affairs of a corporation and was obtained under section 8A or 8B`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "information or document relating to the affairs of a corporation which has been obtained under section 8A or 8B"
    ELSE (IF    `the previous consent in writing of the corporation has been given`
             OR `the publication or disclosure is to the Minister, the Registrar of Companies, their officers or an inspector appointed under Part 9`
             OR `the publication or disclosure is required with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, criminal proceedings pursuant to or arising out of this Act, or criminal proceedings for an offence entailing misconduct in connection with the management of the corporation's affairs or misapplication or wrongful retention of its property`
             OR `the publication or disclosure is required for the purpose of complying with a requirement or exercising a power imposed or conferred by this Act in connection with reports made by inspectors appointed under Part 9`
             OR `the publication or disclosure is required with a view to the institution by the Minister of proceedings for the winding up of the corporation under this Act`
             OR `the publication or disclosure is required for the purpose of proceedings under section 8A or 8B`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, without the previous consent in writing of that corporation, be published or disclosed, except to the Minister, the Registrar of Companies and their officers or to an inspector appointed under Part 9, unless the publication or disclosure is required" (an exception, and an "unless", met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:2730 | (2) A person who publishes or discloses any information or
-- src:2731 | document in contravention of this section shall be guilty of an
-- src:2732 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2733 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2734 | both.
@ref s 8H(2) (src:2730-2734)
GIVEN `the person published or disclosed information or a document in contravention of section 8H` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8H(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person published or disclosed information or a document in contravention of section 8H`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "A person who publishes or discloses any information or document in contravention of this section shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

-- src:2730 | (2) A person who publishes or discloses any information or
-- src:2731 | document in contravention of this section shall be guilty of an
-- src:2732 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2733 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2734 | both.
@ref s 8H(2) (src:2730-2734)
GIVEN `the person published or disclosed information or a document in contravention of section 8H` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 8H(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 8H(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person published or disclosed information or a document in contravention of section 8H` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

DECLARE `s 8H act` IS ONE OF
    `s 8H(1) publish or disclose information or a document obtained under section 8A or 8B, in contravention of section 8H`

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (N2 ruling of 2026-11-04): "A person who publishes or discloses ... in contravention of this section".
-- src:2701 | 8H.—(1) No information or document relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2702 | corporation which has been obtained under section 8A or 8B may,
-- src:2703 | without the previous consent in writing of that corporation, be
-- src:2704 | published or disclosed, except to the Minister, the Registrar of
-- src:2705 | Companies and their officers or to an inspector appointed under
-- src:2706 | Part 9, unless the publication or disclosure is required —
-- src:2730 | (2) A person who publishes or discloses any information or
-- src:2731 | document in contravention of this section shall be guilty of an
-- src:2732 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2733 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2734 | both.
@ref s 8H(2) (src:2701-2734)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8H act`
`s 8H(1) a person must not publish or disclose information or a document obtained under section 8A or 8B` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 8H(1) publish or disclose information or a document obtained under section 8A or 8B, in contravention of section 8H`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person published or disclosed information or a document obtained under section 8A or 8B in contravention of section 8H, which is an offence under section 8H(2)"
